(a) There is created a body corporate and politic, to be known as the South Georgia Regional Information Technology Authority, which shall be a political subdivision of the state and a public corporation and by that name, style, and title said body may contract and be contracted with, bring and defend actions, sue and be sued, implead and be impleaded, and complain and defend in all courts. The authority shall make rules and regulations for its own government and shall have perpetual existence.
